Z||000000||Verticalspeed||12-27-2000||11:31 AM||||If you have a <B>V8 fiero,</B> which <B>Flowmaster Series</B> muffler have you used that bolts in without mods?||||reg||1
Z||000001||BBBAD GT||12-27-2000||01:48 PM||||"bolts in without mods" doesn't exist with a V8 install  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Anyway, I have a late model Fbody flowmaster hooked up to my V8 Fiero, not sure which series it is, but I bet it's most likely the 2 chamber.  Its loud, but not that loud.  Its waaaay too cold here to get on the garage floor and look at the part number on the muffler.  Go to my V8 link below, I took some short movies of it idleing and accelerating, give you and idea of what mine sounds like.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">     <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||V8Fiero||12-27-2000||07:15 PM||||I used thrush "glass packs". Now before anyone says anything, I thought to myself this thing is going to be WAY too loud. I thought that I might have to put resonator tips to mellow the tone but it has a low mellow tone to it. I think it sounds great and they were only $20 each.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Verticalspeed||12-28-2000||01:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BBBAD GT:<BR><B>"bolts in without mods" doesn't exist with a V8 install   <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Is yours carburated or fuel injected? IF carburated, have you ever experienced some hesitation on acceleration? If you did, how did you solve that problem or do you think that is? Fuel pressure too low, too high? too lean, too rich? Position of the throttle pump arm?<BR>Step up springs? Just wondering if you might know the answer. <BR>||||reg||1
